inlineArgWriteT -- SEQ 419 R0 (2026-10-26): docket item (b), testPrecedence's four *Arg rows in minimal form. A compiled caller
hands an inlined callee `*awK` (a holder of awBag["kid"], kid = 7); the callee writes through `argument` with each spelling
testPrecedence's *Arg rows use: `argument = 9`, `argument += 1`, `++argument`, `--argument`. The caller then reads kid.

Today, jitted: AW-1..AW-4 all read 7 -- the write does not reach kid. The interpreted twin (`jitter;` -> `jitterOff;`)
reads 9, 8, 8, 6, which is the intended value (R-C). Silent: every body built 1 called 1.

Controls, which agree today: AW-C, the callee writes a local only (kid 7, local 4). AW-5 and AW-6 hand the callee a PLAIN
field (`awAssignDo(awX)`, `awPlusPlusDo(awX)`) and the write lands (9, 8) -- so the defect needs the starred argument.
